        <section id="en-1">
          <h2>1. Who we are and how to contact us</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>alexandria backup</strong> is a strictly personal-use OAuth application and project, developed and maintained by Pedro Vendramini.
          </p>
          <p>
            For any inquiries, questions, or requests concerning this policy and the application's privacy practices, please contact directly via email: <a href="mailto:pedrovendramini.pv@gmail.com">pedrovendramini.pv@gmail.com</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            This application is neither offered as a commercial service nor distributed for public use; there are no other users other than the owner/maintainer.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="en-2">
          <h2>2. What the application is</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>alexandria backup</strong> is a personal automation tool designed to create encrypted backups of files from the owner's domestic server directly to the owner's own Google Drive cloud storage.
          </p>
          <p>
            The application operates by integrating well-established open-source utilities: <strong>restic</strong> (for chunk-level deduplication and end-to-end client-side encryption) and <strong>rclone</strong> (for cloud synchronization and data transfer via Google APIs).
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="en-3">
          <h2>3. What data we access (and what we do not access)</h2>
          <p>
            The application follows the principle of least privilege:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>What we access:</strong> The application exclusively requests the restricted application data folder OAuth scope (<code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.appdata</code> / <code>drive.appfolder</code>). This scope grants permission to create, read, and write files exclusively within a hidden, dedicated folder created for this application on the owner's Google Drive.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>What we DO NOT access:</strong> The application has <strong>NO access</strong> to files stored in "My Drive", emails (Gmail), contacts, calendar events, photos, Google Docs, or any other private data located in the Google account. The app has zero visibility of files existing outside its designated hidden application folder.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="en-4">
          <h2>4. What we use the data for</h2>
          <p>
            The requested permissions and data are utilized exclusively for one single purpose:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>To enable the application to upload, list, update, and read backup chunks in the hidden application data folder (<code>appdata</code>) in the owner's Google Drive, allowing backup archives to be reliably stored and restored.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            No data is utilized for tracking user behavior, behavioral profiling, machine learning model training, commercial advertising, or any purpose beyond backup synchronization.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="en-5">
          <h2>5. How data is stored and protected</h2>
          <p>
            Data integrity and confidentiality are guaranteed through a zero-knowledge security architecture:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Pre-upload client-side encryption:</strong> All files and directories are encrypted locally on the home server by <em>restic</em> prior to network transmission. Data arrives at Google Drive already completely ciphered.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Locally held keys and tokens:</strong> The restic encryption password/key, along with OAuth authentication tokens, are stored strictly on the owner's local server storage. No keys or tokens are ever uploaded to third-party intermediary servers.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Encrypted transmission:</strong> All network communication with Google's servers takes place over modern, industry-standard encrypted transport layers (HTTPS / TLS).
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="en-6">
          <h2>6. Data sharing</h2>
          <p>
            There is no data sharing whatsoever:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>No sale of data:</strong> No information is sold, rented, or traded under any circumstances.</li>
            <li><strong>No advertising:</strong> There is no advertising, ad tracking, or commercial marketing.</li>
            <li><strong>No third parties:</strong> No data is disclosed to partner companies, brokers, or telemetry vendors.</li>
            <li><strong>No analytics:</strong> The application incorporates no analytics trackers, crash reporting SDKs, or external monitoring software.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="en-7">
          <h2>7. Data retention and deletion</h2>
          <p>
            Backup files remain stored within the hidden application folder on Google Drive for as long as the owner chooses to keep them, based on retention policies defined directly in restic.
          </p>
          <p>
            To delete all data stored by the application or revoke its access at any point in time:
          </p>
          <ol>
            <li>
              <strong>Delete hidden application data in Google Drive:</strong>
              Open Google Drive in your web browser, navigate to <em>Settings</em> (gear icon in the top right) &gt; <em>Manage Apps</em>. Locate <strong>alexandria backup</strong>, click <em>Options</em>, and select <em>Delete hidden app data</em>. This permanently deletes all files created by the application.
            </li>
